BT 1 0 0 1 0 120.09 Tm /F3 10.91 Tf 13.1 TL 1.152969 Tw (This workshop examines how Artificial Intelligence can support research processes, academic writing,) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.122223 Tw (conceptual development, and knowledge production without reducing scholarly work to the automated) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.787879 Tw (generation of texts. Rather than focusing on technical tutorials, the workshop approaches AI as a) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.089245 Tw (methodological and critical interlocutor capable of helping researchers and students formulate better) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.429959 Tw (questions, refine research problems, examine assumptions, organize evidence, compare theoretical) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.03582 Tw (frameworks, generate methodological alternatives, and strengthen argumentation. Special attention will) Tj T* 0 Tw .782233 Tw (be given to the responsible use of AI in academic contexts, including issues of authorship, verification,) Tj T* 0 Tw .708635 Tw (hallucinations, cognitive dependency, ethical use, and the preservation of human judgment. Participants) Tj T* 0 Tw .805507 Tw (will explore how AI can become part of a research workflow while maintaining the intellectual agency) Tj T* 0 Tw (and critical responsibility of the researcher.) Tj T* ET
