BT 1 0 0 1 0 106.99 Tm /F3 10.91 Tf 13.1 TL -0.121285 Tw (This second workshop focuses on the conceptual design of AI-powered assistants, agents, workflows, and) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.416642 Tw (micro-applications with potential use in education, research, administration, professional services, and) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.151608 Tw (entrepreneurship. The workshop does not require programming experience. Its purpose is to help) Tj T* 0 Tw .40462 Tw (participants understand how an idea can move from a simple prompt to an assistant, from an assistant to) Tj T* 0 Tw .282739 Tw (an agent, and from an agent to a possible app or service. Participants will work with a design framework) Tj T* 0 Tw .949573 Tw (for identifying real problems that can be addressed through AI-supported solutions. They will consider) Tj T* 0 Tw .449001 Tw (the intended user, the task to be supported, the knowledge required, the data involved, the ethical limits,) Tj T* 0 Tw .134906 Tw (the role of human supervision, and the possible academic, institutional, or business value of the proposed) Tj T* 0 Tw (solution.) Tj T* ET
